From 8ee1ba32d08b44272eb58a4dd1a7f333175c6497 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Nohdan S." <sbtasm@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:32:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] intel: xmm7360: receive SMS over RPC

The firmware accepts no AT+CPMS storage, so the generic AT messaging
implementation disables itself and incoming SMS are never seen.

Incoming SMS arrive over RPC as UtaMsSmsIncomingIndCb (0x032), carrying
the full PDU (SMSC + TPDU, 176-byte buffer) followed by the TPDU length,
and the host must acknowledge them with UtaMsSmsIncomingSmsAck (0x036),
echoing the indication's transaction id (tipd). The ack layout was
recovered from Lenovo's WinIhvRil.dll:
  B(0) S(176 zero bytes) B(0) L(0) B(tipd) L(0)

Implement the Messaging interface for the XMM7360 RPC modem: MT storage
only (messages live in ModemManager), no-op storage locking, and while
enabled, keep the RPC port open with a handler that parses each
indication, hands the part to the Messaging interface (multipart messages
get assembled there), and acks it.
---
